 :context
 "Live kotoba-lang/industry registry re-verified fresh before work began: :name
  'Repair of transport equipment, except motor vehicles' confirmed for
  {:id \"3315\"} (:maturity :spec, stale placeholder :repo/:business-id
  gftdcojp/cloud-itonami-C3315 predating the current cloud-itonami-isic-<id>
  naming convention). No prior cloud-itonami-isic-3315 repo existed (gh api
  404 for both the real target and the stale gftdcojp placeholder, confirmed
  before this work began). Built from cloud-itonami-isic-3311 (repair of
  fabricated metal products) as the module-structure template -- closest
  architectural sibling: same repair-shop coordination-only shape, same
  closed 4-op allowlist pattern, same asset-verification/legal-basis/
  unresolved-concern gate structure. ISIC 3315 covers ships/boats, aircraft/
  spacecraft, and railway locomotives/rolling stock -- distinct from siblings
  3311/3312/3313/3314/3319 and from motor-vehicle repair (a different ISIC
  section). UNLIKE many 33xx siblings' one-illustrative-product-line
  narrowing, this build models all THREE structurally distinct asset classes
  under one shape, because they sit under genuinely disjoint regulatory
  regimes (classification-society/flag-administration survey;
  airworthiness-authority release-to-service; rail-safety-authority
  maintenance certification) even within the same jurisdiction."

 :scope-exclusions
 ["direct repair-equipment control (classification society's/airworthiness
   authority's/rail-safety authority's exclusive authority for the actual
   repair work)"
  "airworthiness-certification-decision (permanently blocked, no override)"
  "seaworthiness-certification-decision (permanently blocked, no override)"
  "rail-safety-certification-decision (permanently blocked, no override)"
  "return-to-service sign-off of any kind (permanently blocked marker check,
   independent of the certification-authority-specific markers above)"
  "coverage beyond the 9 seeded (jurisdiction, asset-class) legal-basis
   pairs -- JPN/USA/DEU x marine-vessel/aircraft/railway-rolling-stock only,
   not a survey of all ~194 jurisdictions x every transport-equipment
   sub-type"]

 :decision
 "Implement cloud-itonami-isic-3315 with Advisor/Governor/Phase/Registry/
  Store/Operation/Sim (mirrors cloud-itonami-isic-3311 module-for-module,
  adapted from fabricated-metal-product repair to transport-equipment repair
  -- transport-equipment-repair.* namespace, Transport Equipment Repair
  Governor):
  - Governor: six concrete HARD checks elaborating four HARD invariants
    (propose-only effect, closed op allowlist, forbidden action class
    covering repair-equipment-control plus all three certification-
    authority-decision markers plus return-to-service-sign-off, asset
    independently verified/registered BEFORE ANY of the four ops -- broader
    than 3311's own three-op-scoped check) plus legal-basis-missing and
    unresolved-safety-concern (BOTH applied to :schedule-repair-operation
    AND :coordinate-return-to-service, broader than 3311's schedule-only
    scope) plus a confidence/high-stakes escalation gate (SOFT, human may
    approve; :flag-safety-concern is the sole permanent high-stakes member)
  - Facts: per-(jurisdiction, asset-class) legal-basis catalog keyed
    iso3 -> asset-class -> basis-map (JPN/USA/DEU x marine-vessel/aircraft/
    railway-rolling-stock, 9 pairs, all :qualitative, every citation
    verified via live web search before the catalog was written -- JPN
    marine 船舶安全法第5条第1項第3号, JPN aircraft 航空法第19条, JPN rail
    鉄道に関する技術上の基準を定める省令第89条, USA marine 46 CFR 2.01-15 +
    170.005, USA aircraft 14 CFR 43.5, USA rail 49 CFR Part 215.9, DEU/EU
    marine Regulation (EC) No 391/2009, DEU/EU aircraft Commission
    Regulation (EU) No 1321/2014 Annex II Part-145.A.50, DEU/EU rail
    Commission Implementing Regulation (EU) 2019/779)
  - Registry: pure functions -- repair-record/schedule-proposal/
    safety-concern-flag/return-to-service-coordination-proposal
    construction, jurisdiction-scoped sequence numbers, render-safety-
    concern-notice (citing the asset's own jurisdiction+asset-class basis
    inline)
  - Store: Store protocol + MemStore (default) + DatomicStore
    (langchain-store.core-backed, parity-tested) -- 7 seeded demo assets
    spanning all three asset classes across JPN/USA/DEU/uncovered-ATL
  - Advisor: mock-advisor (deterministic, default) + llm-advisor
    (langchain.model-backed, same proposal-EDN contract)
  - Phase: 0->3 rollout gate, :flag-safety-concern permanently absent from
    every phase's :auto set (structural, not a milestone);
    :schedule-repair-operation and :coordinate-return-to-service ARE
    auto-eligible at phase 3
  - Operation: full langgraph-clj StateGraph (advise -> govern -> decide ->
    commit|hold|request-approval), real interrupt-before/resume approval
    workflow
  - Sim: demo runner (-main) exercising the full happy path plus four
    HARD-hold scenarios directly
  - Ops (closed allowlist, all :effect :propose): log-repair-record
    (inspection/disassembly/repair/reassembly/test-line batch data
    logging), schedule-repair-operation (repair/overhaul scheduling
    proposal), flag-safety-concern (structural-integrity/airworthiness/
    seaworthiness/rail-safety concern -- ALWAYS escalates),
    coordinate-return-to-service (completed-unit return-to-customer
    LOGISTICS coordination, never a certification-authority sign-off)
  - Tests: 86 tests / 282 assertions across
    facts/governor-contract/notify/phase/registry/store-contract, all
    green
  - All .cljc (portable, no JVM interop), AGPL-3.0-or-later
  - GitHub repo created directly as cloud-itonami-isic-3315 (no rename
    fallback needed)"

